s role, he also addresses the ethical aspects of nutrition and hydration in children, contributing to a comprehensive understanding of these critical issues in pediatric care.", "TRATAMIENTO EN GASTROENTEROLOGÍA, HEPATOLOGÍA Y NUTRICIÓN PEDIÁTRICA:A comprehensive treatment guide that includes enteral nutrition as a key component for managing pediatric gastroenterological and nutritional issues.", "TABLAS:The entity \"TABLAS\" refers to tables included in a document that serve multiple purposes related to nutrition. These tables provide diagnostic parameters for assessing the severity of malnutrition, offering essential criteria for evaluation. Additionally, they outline the main indications for enteral nutrition in pediatrics, detailing various medical conditions and their corresponding nutritional requirements. Together, these tables serve as a comprehensive resource for understanding and addressing nutritional needs in both malnutrition assessment and enteral nutrition guidance for pediatric patients.", "DIFICULTADES PARA LA INGESTIÓN:A category of conditions that impede the ability to ingest food, necessitating enteral nutrition in pediatric patients.", "DIFICULTADES PARA LA DIGESTIÓN Y ABSORCIÓN:A category of conditions that affect digestion and nutrient absorption, often requiring enteral nutrition interventions in pediatric care.", "ENFERMEDADES EXTRADIGESTIVAS:A category of diseases outside the digestive system that can increase nutritional requirements, often necessitating enteral nutrition in pediatric patients."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}